# Opus variant, classifier rename 1 of 5 (see README.md in this
# directory). Part of a matched set with the opus72 transplant in
# transplants.txt here: never apply the renames without it.
name: opus-rename-classifier-mod0-copy1
kind: module
module: 0
region: data
address: 0x030056C7
gate: Never apply without the opus72 transplant (patches/opus_swap/
  transplants.txt): the rename routes extension OPU to decoder
  module 72, which holds the WMA library until the transplant
  replaces it. Build refuses unless the 3 stock bytes at the target
  equal expect; the finished image must also pass
  firmware_patch.validate().
rationale: First of three copies of the audio extension classifier
  string MP1MP2MP3WMAWAVAPEFLAAACM4AOGGMP43GPDFFDSF in module 0
  data; the WMA entry sits at string offset +9. Renaming it to OPU
  makes slot 3 match the extension the FAT layer's 8.3 alias
  carries for .opus files, so Opus files reach decoder module 72
  through the stock selection path, and .wma files stop matching.
  No direct code reference to this copy was found; it is renamed
  for consistency with the other copies, as the donor project
  renamed all of its copies.
expect: 574d41
replace: 4f5055
